{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && cat > update-13.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The snapshot-boundary line is closed with a retained control, but one saved Fact from the earlier five-node attempt is now known to be founded on a false premise and is still stored uncorrected. This update revises that Fact in place (same id) instead of adding another standalone note, and records the lineage so a reviewer does not rely on the superseded statement.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-compact13\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 216, \\\"end_line\\\": 262, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl13\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 220, \\\"end_line\\\": 300, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-lastindex13\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"state.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 157, \\\"end_line\\\": 174, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@q-knowledge-lineage\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Which saved claims about the five-node reachability history are superseded by the sealed-partition control, and are they revised in place rather than duplicated?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact13\\\", \\\"src-repl13\\\", \\\"src-lastindex13\\\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"7465f7b9e6cd44e39e8cbf7e2c45c955-knowledge-0\\\",\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n      \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Revised: the earlier claim that a legal five-node history reaches the snapshot-boundary precondition but the follower does not stay unrepairable was produced by a harness whose partition cut only the leader<->majority links, leaving the partner<->majority path open; the partner was therefore repaired by the successor during the partition and was already at store 1..4 by the time of the heal, which is why that run showed zero Restore calls. With the partition sealed on both sides the same history keeps the stale suffix and the follower is unrepairable: the retained control receipt beca431464bf44ab9c3354145c21899f shows the TrailingLogs=0 case installing the same snapshot 687-697 times with the follower's applied index pinned at the snapshot index 4 and its advertised last index stuck at 7, while the TrailingLogs=3 case with an otherwise identical history converges with zero snapshot installs (applied and last index both 4). The earlier statement must not be relied on; only the sealed-partition results and the single-peer witness remain valid.\\\",\n      \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"Same harness family: five bootstrapped nodes in one process over InmemTransport/InmemStore, two-sided partition of {leader, partner} from the other three peers, TrailingLogs 0 versus 3, equal 1 s timeouts; frozen snapshot fd2d6988362c434e9fda87b87c5fb0df.\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact13\\\", \\\"src-repl13\\\", \\\"src-lastindex13\\\"],\n      \\\"changed_premise\\\": \\\"The old Fact assumed the partner had been isolated during the partition; it had not, because only leader<->majority links were disconnected, so the observed convergence reflected the partner never leaving the majority's reach rather than an enclosing protection against the loop.\\\",\n      \\\"affected_uses\\\": [\n        \\\"7465f7b9e6cd44e39e8cbf7e2c45c955-question-0\\\",\n        \\\"7465f7b9e6cd44e39e8cbf7e2c45c955-interpretation-0\\\",\n        \\\"e4d33475358149f5b10619d6df4b1e3b-question-0\\\",\n        \\\"e4d33475358149f5b10619d6df4b1e3b-gap-3\\\",\n        \\\"b836c3a8cfc549188ebed6183f15f019-knowledge-0\\\",\n        \\\"542e6bce20cb456fb6a01a29002f7cc4-question-0\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"executions\\\": { \\\"beca431464bf44ab9c3354145c21899f\\\": [9, 19] }\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-knowledge-lineage\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact13\\\", \\\"src-repl13\\\", \\\"src-lastindex13\\\"],\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"explained\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The lineage is now coherent and no claim rests on the superseded run. Sequence: the first five-node harness reported convergence with zero Restore calls and no snapshot install, which was read as ordinary repair closing the gap and used to narrow the leader-side loop; the sealed-partition rerun showed the loop with 668-697 installs and a pinned applied index; the paired control then showed that only compaction depth distinguishes loop from convergence (TrailingLogs=0 loops, TrailingLogs=3 converges), and the earlier run's cause was identified as an incomplete partition that left the partner reachable from the majority. Consequently the Fact 7465f7b9e6cd44e39e8cbf7e2c45c955-knowledge-0 is revised in place above, the standalone correction note from an earlier batch is superseded by that revision, and the narrowing argument that rested on the old Fact is withdrawn: the leader-side loop's reachability stands for the sealed-partition, leader-compacted-past-the-boundary conditions evidenced by CheckRun f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30 and the control CheckRun beca431464bf44ab9c3354145c21899f. No new measurement is claimed here; this entry records which stored assertion changed, why, and what a reviewer should rely on.\\\",\n      \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n        { \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"7465f7b9e6cd44e39e8cbf7e2c45c955-knowledge-0\\\", \\\"revision\\\": 2, \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"sealed-partition results replace the earlier convergence claim\\\" }\n      ],\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The superseded run is retained at CheckRun b9b56ddf3d7d43319db460b87846f71f and its cause is explained there; it is not deleted, but it is no longer evidence about reachability.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The revision is limited to the five-node in-process configuration actually executed; default TrailingLogs and network transports remain unsampled.\\\",\n        \\\"This entry does not re-measure anything; it only corrects the stored premise and its dependents.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-13.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
